WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.580
So there's been a lot of discussion of if
and when Joe Biden is going to denounce violence

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.400
that is taking place in different places around
the country.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.610
And the Trumpet's and Donald Trump himself
have focused in a lot on this.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.890
Why won't Joe Biden denounce this?

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.700
Why won't Joe Biden denounce that?

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.949
Now, before we get to the sort of substance
here, which is that Joe Biden did it and a

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:29.910
lot of people on the left are furious with
him and the right is just simply ignoring

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:30.910
it.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.910
Does Joe Biden really need to denounce anything
in the sense that we currently have violence

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.930
happening under the leadership of Donald Trump
and even though Donald Trump is trying to

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.780
insist that violence is what's in store in
Biden's America?

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.420
Do you look back at when Biden was vice president,
things were relatively calm.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:54.379
And the violence that we are seeing now to
the extent that it exists is a lot of it is

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:56.190
being done by Trump supporters.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.930
Of course, not all of it, but it is all happening
as Donald Trump is president of the United

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.930
States.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:05.449
But OK, let's put that we'll table that argument
for now.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:10.000
And let's just say people want Biden to denounce
the violence.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Well, he did it.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.700
Joe Biden did it in a speech in Pennsylvania.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.700
And Trump lists are just pretending that he
didn't do it.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.289
And some of the left is furious.

00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:24.450
So what I want to discuss with you after we
look at the Clippers, did this make sense?

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.850
Let's take a look at what Joe Biden had to
say.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.359
Rioting is not protesting.

00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:31.689
Looting is not protesting.

00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:33.719
Setting fires is not protesting.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:37.009
None of this is protesting.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:38.149
It's lawlessness.

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:39.969
Plain and simple.

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:43.639
And those who do it should be prosecuted.

00:01:43.639 --> 00:01:47.999
Violence will not bring change and only bring
destruction.

00:01:47.999 --> 00:01:49.840
It's wrong in every way.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:56.000
It divides instead of unites, destroys businesses,
only hurts the working families that serve

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.340
the community.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.450
It makes things worse across the board, not
better.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.559
No, it's not what Dr. King or John Lewis taught.

00:02:04.559 --> 00:02:05.599
And it must.

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:08.920
And so on the facts.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.379
I agree with Joe Biden here.

00:02:11.379 --> 00:02:13.090
Rioting is not protesting.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.090
Looting is not protesting.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.870
And setting fires is not protesting in the
sense that it will bring productive change.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:22.599
Now, I know that there are people who will
respond and say you don't get to set the terms

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.650
of what counts as protesting.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.370
OK, well, we'll get to that in a little bit.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.830
But the possible folly of Joe Biden doing
this is that the right is just pretending

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:32.830
he didn't do it.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:38.129
They're continuing to say, why won't Joe Biden
denounce violence even though he's done it?

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:42.450
And there's a slice of the left that is absolutely
furious with Joe Biden here.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.500
Now, I'm not saying it's all the left or a
huge portion, but it's certainly a very loud

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.420
slice of the left, particularly online.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.720
And the reason that some on the left are mad
at Joe Biden for doing this is they say that

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:01.099
he's playing into the idea that it's his supporters
who are being violent.

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:06.230
Yet the idea being by Joe Biden coming out
and saying, no matter who's doing it, I'm

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:07.519
against the violence.

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:14.840
It sort of frames it up as Joe Biden acknowledging
that it is his supporters being violent and

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.700
telling them to stop.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.450
I think that there are two sides to this.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:27.430
So, first of all, I find it completely reasonable
and unproblematic that Joe Biden says violence

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.680
is bad and I'm against it.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.950
It's insane that it has to be said.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:37.959
But he said it and he said, no matter who
does the violence, I'm against the violence.

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:42.659
But the second piece is that it's important
to clarify at every opportunity that almost

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:48.260
nobody on the left is being violent, that
a lot of the violence is provocateurs and

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.349
right wingers.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:56.790
And I hate to say this, but by and large,
the leftists that are being violent are overwhelmingly

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.129
not people supporting Joe Biden.

00:03:59.129 --> 00:04:04.790
And often individuals who see Joe Biden as
as much of a problem or almost as much of

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.709
a problem as Donald Trump.

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:15.870
So if there is a criticism of Joe Biden here,
it's that he arguably, indirectly or implicitly

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.120
seems to be acknowledging or conceding that
some of his supporters are being violent.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.310
And I really don't think that that's the case
at all.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.890
I've not really seen evidence of that.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:28.690
So I don't believe there's any problem with
Joe Biden denouncing violence in principle.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:33.130
I do think it's sort of like when, you know,
there is an Islamic terror attack and right

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:37.630
wingers start saying, why didn't this individual
Muslim person who had nothing to do with it

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.289
denounced the violence?

00:04:39.289 --> 00:04:43.069
Well, most people denounce violence implicitly.

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:44.479
Most people are against violence.

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:50.180
I don't know whether that is even something
that should be expected, particularly when

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.389
Joe Biden isn't in power and there's no evidence
that it is his supporters that are doing anything.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.699
But what I would like to see more of is Joe
Biden aggressively placing the blame where

00:04:58.699 --> 00:04:59.720
it should be placed.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.919
Biden should be saying or let me go back.

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:08.750
There are people saying by doing this, Joe
Biden is hinting that he's going to police

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.949
and limit protests as president and limit
free speech.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:15.340
That's not at all what Biden is doing here.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:20.470
And in fact, the Obama Biden administration
had a completely normal relationship with

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:21.819
the press.

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:28.030
Trump is the one that's authoritarian and
dystopian when it comes to a free press.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:35.800
And ultimately, this is a sort of discussion
of the Martin Luther King perspective on protests

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.389
versus the Malcolm X perspective.

00:05:38.389 --> 00:05:44.610
And one of the things that most resonates
with me that Dr. King often said was the problem

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:52.230
with going to looting, arson, violence as
a form of protest is not whether it's morally

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:53.660
defensible.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.660
Maybe it is.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.620
That's a perfectly reasonable conversation
to have.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:03.840
But the small percentage who choose to do
it often end up hurting themselves.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:10.720
And when protests go to violence, looting,
et cetera, it very often backfires and hurts

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.750
the very people that we are trying to help
through our activism.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.220
That was this is Martin Luther King's view.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.990
And you can extensively find interviews with
him on YouTube where he says that.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.960
That's my take on it.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.860
So on the facts, I do tend to agree with Joe
Biden.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.530
I think the framing of Biden must announced.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.530
Biden must denounce.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.530
He does.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:34.090
And they just keep saying Biden must announce
his if he didn't do it.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.130
That's where it starts to get a little problematic.

